            <ArticleTitle>Double retroaortic left renal veins as a possible cause of pelvic congestion syndrome: imaging findings in two patients.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>e152-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Pelvic congestion syndrome is characterized by chronic pelvic pain and varicose veins around the uterus and ovaries. We report two cases of double retroaortic left renal vein, associated with left-sided pelvic congestion syndrome, diagnosed by CT and confirmed by clinical findings and colour Doppler ultrasound. Double retroaortic left renal veins may be a contributing factor for the development of left pelvic congestion syndrome. This is the first report of double retroaortic left renal vein and associated pelvic congestion syndrome.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
